{
  "_comment": [
    "The Shuffle lane's live tuning (MODES.md 59l). Published to config/shuffle by",
    "firebase/seed/seed-shuffle.mjs, which refuses anything the game would refuse. Every device",
    "reads it beside play and opens its next run on it; a device that cannot reach the server",
    "plays the last one it read, or the build's own figures.",
    "",
    "To retune: change figures, raise `revision` by one, run `node firebase/seed/seed-shuffle.mjs",
    "--check`, then without --check. Every figure is a whole number. Each moves only inside its",
    "range (a card's figures from a quarter to four times what ships, a card's `most` up to twice);",
    "the tool names the range when a figure is outside it.",
    "",
    "Hundredths: a key ending in Hundredths is a time, a share or a width times 100 (150 = 1.5 s).",
    "Tenths: a key ending in Tenths is tenths of the bolt, of the march or of a fuel tube.",
    "A card's figures are in the units of its row in ShuffleCards.All. A figure the card's text",
    "states in words (a count, a time, 'half') is fixed and refused if moved; a per cent the text",
    "prints follows the figure on every phone. `enabled: false` takes a card out of every hand.",
    "",
    "The deep surge (ramp.surge*): from surgeFromWave, every wave multiplies raider health and blow",
    "by a per cent (surgeHealthPercent, surgeBlowPercent) that grows by its ...Step every",
    "surgeEveryWaves waves. Health stops at 5,000x (a code limit, not a figure); from the wave after,",
    "raiders walk faster the same way (surgePacePercent, ...Step) up to surgePaceMostHundredths (500 = 5x,",
    "at most 600). A per cent and its step both at 0 switch that part off. Cards are never touched.",
    "",
    "Cannot be tuned here: a hand's size and how often one is owed (written into the lane's own",
    "text in nine languages), the star waves (they pay coins), and anything outside Shuffle.",
    "To return every device to its build's own figures: delete config/shuffle.",
    "",
    "The refresh price (refresh.*, MODES.md 59p): the first refresh of a run costs firstGems (0 sells",
    "none), and each one bought multiplies the next by factorHundredths (200 doubles, 100 holds it)."
  ],

